# Deploy-time artifacts — must not be baked into the image.
#
# deploy.sh writes public/config.json (Cognito IDs for the live stack) and harvests
# the CloudXR.js React sample into public/cloudxr/, then uploads public/ to S3.
# CloudFront serves that content from S3 — the image only needs the fallback login
# page. Excluding them here does not affect the S3 upload, which reads from disk.
#
# Baking them in would: add ~67MB to the image, embed Cognito IDs belonging to
# whatever stack was last deployed, and make the image depend on local state — so a
# fresh clone would produce a different image than a machine that had already run
# deploy.sh. The build must be reproducible from a clean checkout.
public/cloudxr/
public/config.json

# Local dependency tree — npm install runs inside the image
node_modules/
npm-debug.log

# Not needed at runtime
build-proxy.sh
.dockerignore
